{"title":"VEnron: A versioned spreadsheet corpus and related evolution analysis","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2889160.2889238","doi":"10.1145/2889160.2889238","authors":["Wensheng Dou","Liang Xu","Shing Chi Cheung","Chushu Gao","Jun Wei","Tao Huang"],"year":2016,"published":"2016-05-14","abstract":"Presents a semi-automated method that combines spreadsheet contents, filenames, and spreadsheet-attached emails to identify evolved spreadsheets and recover fragmented version information in the Enron email archive. The resulting VEnron corpus supports empirical analysis of formula changes and errors introduced during spreadsheet evolution.","venue":"5th International Workshop on Green and Sustainable Software (GREENS 2016), ICSE Companion"}
{"title":"SpreadCluster: Recovering Versioned Spreadsheets through Similarity-Based Clustering","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1704.08476","arxiv_id":"1704.08476","doi":"10.1109/MSR.2017.28","authors":["Liang Xu","Wensheng Dou","Chushu Gao","Jie Wang","Jun Wei","Hua Zhong","Tao Huang"],"year":2017,"published":"2017-04-27","abstract":"Learns similarity criteria such as worksheet-name and table-header features from known version groups and uses them to cluster spreadsheets likely to be versions of the same evolving artifact. It is evaluated on Enron spreadsheets and additional spreadsheet corpora and is used to construct the VEnron2 versioned corpus.","venue":"14th IEEE/ACM International Conference on Mining Software Repositories (MSR 2017)"}
{"title":"SheetDiff: A Tool for Identifying Changes in Spreadsheets","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/VLHCC.2010.21","doi":"10.1109/VLHCC.2010.21","authors":["Chris Chambers","Martin Erwig","Markus Luckey"],"year":2010,"abstract":"Introduces SheetDiff for identifying changes between spreadsheet versions rather than relying on raw cell-coordinate comparison. The work targets spreadsheet evolution and reuse and demonstrates a prototype for exposing structural changes between related sheets.","venue":"IEEE Symposium on Visual Languages and Human-Centric Computing (VL/HCC 2010)"}
{"title":"Planted-model evaluation of algorithms for identifying differences between spreadsheets","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/VLHCC.2012.6344471","doi":"10.1109/VLHCC.2012.6344471","authors":["Anna Harutyunyan","Glencora Borradaile","Christopher Chambers","Christopher Scaffidi"],"year":2012,"abstract":"Presents RowColAlign, a two-dimensional generalization of longest-common-subsequence alignment for finding differences between spreadsheets, and a planted model for evaluating spreadsheet differencing algorithms. The evaluation explicitly includes comparison with SheetDiff and targets comparison of spreadsheet versions.","venue":"IEEE Symposium on Visual Languages and Human-Centric Computing (VL/HCC 2012)"}
{"title":"Detecting table clones and smells in spreadsheets","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2950290.2950359","doi":"10.1145/2950290.2950359","authors":["Wensheng Dou","Shing-Chi Cheung","Chushu Gao","Chang Xu","Liang Xu","Jun Wei"],"year":2016,"published":"2016-11-01","abstract":"Introduces TableCheck for matching spreadsheet tables using header information and detecting inconsistent corresponding cells among table clones. The empirical evaluation studies spreadsheets in the EUSES corpus and provides evidence about correspondence among copied and independently evolving spreadsheet regions.","venue":"24th ACM SIGSOFT International Symposium on Foundations of Software Engineering (FSE 2016)"}
{"title":"A bidirectional model-driven spreadsheet environment","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ICSE.2012.6227073","doi":"10.1109/ICSE.2012.6227073","authors":["Jácome Cunha","João Paulo Fernandes","Jorge Mendes","João Saraiva"],"year":2012,"abstract":"Presents a model-driven spreadsheet environment in which spreadsheet models and spreadsheet data can co-evolve bidirectionally. Changes to the model can be propagated to spreadsheets and structural changes made in spreadsheets can be reflected back into their models.","venue":"34th International Conference on Software Engineering (ICSE 2012)"}
{"title":"MDSheet: A framework for model-driven spreadsheet engineering","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ICSE.2012.6227239","doi":"10.1109/ICSE.2012.6227239","authors":["Jácome Cunha","João Paulo Fernandes","Jorge Mendes","João Saraiva"],"year":2012,"abstract":"Describes a framework for embedding higher-level models in spreadsheets and supporting model inference and evolution. It provides structural machinery relevant to preserving spreadsheet organization through controlled evolution.","venue":"34th International Conference on Software Engineering (ICSE 2012)"}
{"title":"Where-provenance for bidirectional editing in spreadsheets","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cola.2022.101155","doi":"10.1016/j.cola.2022.101155","authors":["Jack Williams","Andy Gordon"],"year":2022,"abstract":"Introduces portals, spreadsheet values paired with where-provenance links to one or more origin locations. Provenance is propagated through formulas so that a computed cell can retain links to source locations and support bidirectional editing; the authors also analyze compatibility with functions from a widely used commercial spreadsheet system.","venue":"Journal of Computer Languages"}
{"title":"Detecting and visualizing inter-worksheet smells in spreadsheets","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ICSE.2012.6227171","doi":"10.1109/ICSE.2012.6227171","authors":["Felienne Hermans","Martin Pinzger","Arie van Deursen"],"year":2012,"abstract":"Analyzes dependencies between worksheets and proposes inter-worksheet smells and visualizations for identifying problematic workbook structure. The approach is evaluated on spreadsheet corpora and industrial case studies, providing empirical evidence for workbook-level dependency analysis.","venue":"34th International Conference on Software Engineering (ICSE 2012)"}
{"title":"Inferring templates from spreadsheets","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/1134285.1134312","doi":"10.1145/1134285.1134312","authors":["Robin Abraham","Martin Erwig"],"year":2006,"published":"2006-05-28","abstract":"Presents automatic inference of higher-level spreadsheet templates from existing spreadsheets. The method recovers structural relationships that are implicit in cell layouts and formulas and is evaluated against human-derived spreadsheet structures.","venue":"28th International Conference on Software Engineering (ICSE 2006)"}
{"title":"Header and Unit Inference for Spreadsheets Through Spatial Analyses","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/VLHCC.2004.29","doi":"10.1109/VLHCC.2004.29","authors":["Robin Abraham","Martin Erwig"],"year":2004,"abstract":"Presents spatial-analysis algorithms for inferring spreadsheet headers and units and integrates them into an implemented system. The work empirically evaluates recovery of semantic roles that are encoded implicitly through spreadsheet layout.","venue":"IEEE Symposium on Visual Languages and Human-Centric Computing (VL/HCC 2004)"}
{"title":"Reasoning about spreadsheets with labels and dimensions","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jvlc.2010.08.004","doi":"10.1016/j.jvlc.2010.08.004","authors":["Chris Chambers","Martin Erwig"],"year":2010,"abstract":"Combines spatial relationships between labels and cells with units-of-measurement constraints to infer semantic properties of spreadsheet formulas. The integrated analysis is evaluated for formula-error detection and demonstrates that spreadsheet layout and dimensional semantics provide complementary evidence.","venue":"Journal of Visual Languages & Computing"}
{"title":"Finding high-level structures in spreadsheet programs","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/WCRE.2002.1173080","doi":"10.1109/WCRE.2002.1173080","authors":["Roland T. Mittermeir","Markus Clermont"],"year":2002,"abstract":"Studies recovery of higher-level structures from spreadsheet programs whose computation is otherwise represented at the cell level. The work is motivated by spreadsheet maintenance and evolution and provides structural abstractions for reasoning about formula regions and repeated computational patterns.","venue":"Working Conference on Reverse Engineering (WCRE 2002)"}
{"title":"Extracting implicit tree structures in spreadsheet calculation","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/00140139108964845","doi":"10.1080/00140139108964845","authors":["Pertti Saariluoma","Jorma Sajaniemi"],"year":1991,"abstract":"Empirically studies how implicit computational structures are extracted from spreadsheet calculations. Experiments involving multiple spreadsheet types provide early evidence that spreadsheet computations possess higher-level hierarchical organization beyond individual cells.","venue":"Ergonomics"}
{"title":"TableSense: Spreadsheet Table Detection with Convolutional Neural Networks","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.13500","arxiv_id":"2106.13500","doi":"10.1609/aaai.v33i01.330169","authors":["Haoyu Dong","Shijie Liu","Shi Han","Zhouyu Fu","Dongmei Zhang"],"year":2019,"abstract":"Detects table regions in spreadsheets using cell-level features, convolutional modeling, and active learning. The method is evaluated on a large collection of worksheets and preserves spreadsheet spatial organization rather than flattening sheets to CSV-like tables.","venue":"AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence"}
{"title":"SpreadsheetLLM: Encoding Spreadsheets for Large Language Models","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.09025","arxiv_id":"2407.09025","authors":["Yuzhang Tian","Jianbo Zhao","Haoyu Dong","Junyu Xiong","Shiyu Xia","Mengyu Zhou","Yun Lin","José Cambronero","Yeye He","Shi Han","Dongmei Zhang"],"year":2024,"published":"2024-07-12","abstract":"Proposes spreadsheet encodings and compression schemes intended to preserve important layout and formatting structure while making large sheets tractable for language models. The representation is evaluated on spreadsheet table detection and question answering, providing single-version representation evidence rather than cross-version lineage."}
{"title":"ClassSheets: automatic generation of spreadsheet applications from object-oriented specifications","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/1101908.1101929","doi":"10.1145/1101908.1101929","authors":["Gregor Engels","Martin Erwig"],"year":2005,"abstract":"Introduces an object-oriented specification language for representing spreadsheet structure at a level above individual cells and automatically generating spreadsheet applications from those specifications. It provides an early formal representation of repeated and hierarchical spreadsheet structures.","venue":"20th IEEE/ACM International Conference on Automated Software Engineering (ASE 2005)"}
{"title":"CUSTODES: Automatic spreadsheet cell clustering and smell detection using strong and weak features","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2884781.2884796","doi":"10.1145/2884781.2884796","authors":["Shing Chi Cheung","Wanjun Chen","Yepang Liu","Chang Xu"],"year":2016,"abstract":"Clusters spreadsheet cells using strong and weak structural features and performs smell detection within the resulting groups. Its evaluation demonstrates automated recovery of semantically related cell regions despite variation in spreadsheet tabulation styles.","venue":"IEEE/ACM International Conference on Software Engineering Companion (ICSE 2016)"}
{"title":"Detecting Changes in XML Documents","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ICDE.2002.994696","doi":"10.1109/ICDE.2002.994696","authors":["Grégory Cobéna","Serge Abiteboul","Amélie Marian"],"year":2002,"abstract":"Presents an XML differencing method that uses persistent node identifiers to track document components across versions and represents insertions, deletions, updates, and subtree moves. The method is empirically evaluated on synthetic data and web-derived XML documents and provides direct structured-document evidence for persistent element identity.","venue":"18th International Conference on Data Engineering (ICDE 2002)"}
{"title":"X-Diff: An Effective Change Detection Algorithm for XML Documents","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ICDE.2003.1260818","doi":"10.1109/ICDE.2003.1260818","year":2003,"abstract":"Introduces a change-detection algorithm for unordered XML trees that matches elements and generates edit scripts between document versions. The method is experimentally compared with prior XML differencing approaches and provides transfer evidence for structural correspondence under document revision.","venue":"19th International Conference on Data Engineering (ICDE 2003)"}
{"title":"XChange: A semantic diff approach for XML documents","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.is.2020.101610","doi":"10.1016/j.is.2020.101610","year":2020,"abstract":"Targets semantic understanding of changes between sequential versions of the same XML document. XChange first establishes element correspondences using keys or similarity and then aggregates syntactic edits into coarse-grained semantic changes; it is experimentally compared with XML diff approaches.","venue":"Information Systems"}
{"title":"Class-Agnostic Region-of-Interest Matching in Document Images","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.21055","arxiv_id":"2506.21055","authors":["Demin Zhang","Jiahao Lyu","Zhijie Shen","Yu Zhou"],"year":2025,"published":"2025-06-26","abstract":"Defines a document-image task in which a user-selected reference region must be matched to the corresponding region in another target document image. The proposed benchmark covers multiple difficulty levels and the baseline uses Siamese feature extraction and cross-attention to align semantically similar regions at multiple granularities."}
{"title":"Document Image Verification Based on Paragraph Alignment and Subtle Change Detection","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/app152312430","doi":"10.3390/app152312430","authors":["Daoquan Li","Weifei Jia","Quanlin Yu","Zhaoxu Hu"],"year":2025,"published":"2025-11-23","abstract":"Compares an input document image against a corresponding reference document by retrieving the reference, aligning paragraphs using structural features, and detecting subtle content changes under print-scan distortions. Experiments on constructed document-image databases evaluate both correspondence and change detection.","venue":"Applied Sciences"}
{"title":"Semi-structured document image matching and recognition","url":"https://doi.org/10.1117/12.2003911","doi":"10.1117/12.2003911","authors":["Olivier Augereau","Nicholas Journet","Jean-Philippe Domenger"],"year":2013,"abstract":"Studies matching, recognition, and localization of semi-structured document images using techniques adapted from visual object recognition. The method addresses repeated textual patterns and variable layouts, making it relevant transfer evidence for document-region correspondence.","venue":"Proceedings of SPIE"}
{"title":"Matching document images with ground truth","url":"https://dblp.org/rec/journals/moc/Hobby98","authors":["John D. Hobby"],"year":1998,"abstract":"Develops methods for aligning document images with electronic ground-truth representations so that source information can be associated with positions in scanned images. The work is an early document-image alignment foundation for transferring logical or textual annotations to image coordinates.","venue":"International Journal on Document Analysis and Recognition"}
{"title":"Automated Ground Truth Data Generation for Newspaper Document Images","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/ICDAR.2009.214","doi":"10.1109/ICDAR.2009.214","authors":["Thomas Strecker","Joost van Beusekom","Sahin Albayrak","Thomas M. Breuel"],"year":2009,"abstract":"Generates electronic newspaper documents together with geometric and logical layout ground truth, then aligns printed-and-scanned versions with the synthetic originals. Estimated transformations are used to map layout-component coordinates from the electronic version into the scanned document image.","venue":"10th International Conference on Document Analysis and Recognition (ICDAR 2009)"}
{"title":"The T-Recs Table Recognition and Analysis System","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-48172-9_21","doi":"10.1007/3-540-48172-9_21","authors":["Thomas Kieninger","Andreas Dengel"],"abstract":"Presents a bottom-up table structure recognizer that clusters word segments, constructs a tile structure, and recovers row- and column-spanning cells as well as sparse tables. It is designed to work across mixed-mode documents and low-quality OCR, making it foundational evidence for preserving nontrivial table topology.","venue":"Document Analysis Systems: Theory and Practice"}
{"title":"Split, Embed and Merge: An accurate table structure recognizer","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.patcog.2022.108565","doi":"10.1016/j.patcog.2022.108565","authors":["Zhenrong Zhang","Jianshu Zhang","Jun Du","Fengren Wang"],"year":2022,"abstract":"Introduces a multimodal table structure recognizer that splits table images into fine grids, embeds visual and textual information, and merges grids to recover cells including complex spanning structures. It is evaluated on public table-structure benchmarks and directly operates on table images.","venue":"Pattern Recognition"}
{"title":"Robust Table Detection and Structure Recognition from Heterogeneous Document Images","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.patcog.2022.109006","doi":"10.1016/j.patcog.2022.109006","authors":["Chixiang Ma","Weihong Lin","Lei Sun","Qiang Huo"],"year":2023,"abstract":"Introduces RobusTabNet for table localization and reconstruction of cellular topology from heterogeneous document images. Its split-and-merge recognizer explicitly recovers spanning cells and is evaluated on several public benchmarks plus challenging tables with large blank areas and geometric distortion.","venue":"Pattern Recognition"}
{"title":"Finding the Evidence: Localization-aware Answer Prediction for Text Visual Question Answering","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2010.02582","arxiv_id":"2010.02582","doi":"10.18653/v1/2020.coling-main.278","authors":["Wei Han","Hantao Huang","Tao Han"],"year":2020,"published":"2020-10-06","abstract":"Augments text visual question answering with explicit localization of the visual evidence supporting an answer. The model jointly predicts answers and evidence bounding boxes and is empirically evaluated on multiple text-oriented visual QA benchmarks.","venue":"COLING 2020"}
{"title":"BBox DocVQA: A Large Scale Bounding Box Grounded Dataset for Enhancing Reasoning in Document Visual Question Answer","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.15090","arxiv_id":"2511.15090","authors":["Wenhan Yu","Wang Chen","Guanqiang Qi","Weikang Li","Yang Li","Lei Sha","Deguo Xia","Jizhou Huang"],"year":2025,"published":"2025-11-19","abstract":"Introduces a DocVQA dataset in which each question-answer instance is grounded to explicit bounding boxes rather than only a page or document. It includes single- and multi-region and single- and multi-page examples, uses human verification, and evaluates both localization and answer reasoning."}
{"title":"CLTR: An End-to-End, Transformer-Based System for Cell Level Table Retrieval and Table Question Answering","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2106.04441","arxiv_id":"2106.04441","authors":["Feifei Pan","Mustafa Canim","Michael Glass","Alfio Gliozzo","Peter Fox"],"year":2021,"published":"2021-06-08","abstract":"Combines table retrieval and table question answering with localization of relevant table cells. It produces cell-level relevance information and evaluates end-to-end retrieval and answering, providing fine-grained provenance evidence on pre-extracted tables."}
{"title":"TACR: A Table-alignment-based Cell-selection and Reasoning Model for Hybrid Question-Answering","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.14682","arxiv_id":"2305.14682","authors":["Jian Wu","Yicheng Xu","Yan Gao","Jian-Guang Lou","Börje F. Karlsson","Manabu Okumura"],"year":2023,"published":"2023-05-24","abstract":"Uses table alignment and explicit cell selection before reasoning over hybrid table-and-text questions. Evaluation on table QA benchmarks provides evidence for fine-grained identification of cells supporting an answer, although the tables are already structurally available."}
{"title":"Multi-Page Document Visual Question Answering using Self-Attention Scoring Mechanism","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.19024","arxiv_id":"2404.19024","doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-70552-6_13","authors":["Lei Kang","Rubèn Tito","Ernest Valveny","Dimosthenis Karatzas"],"year":2024,"published":"2024-04-29","abstract":"Addresses multi-page DocVQA by assigning relevance scores to pages and selecting pertinent pages before answer generation. Experiments study document collections containing many pages, providing empirical page-level evidence localization but not exact region or cell provenance.","venue":"International Conference on Document Analysis and Recognition (ICDAR 2024)"}
{"title":"Doc-V*: Coarse-to-Fine Interactive Visual Reasoning for Multi-Page Document VQA","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.13731","arxiv_id":"2604.13731","authors":["Yuanlei Zheng","Pei Fu","Hang Li","Ziyang Wang","Yuyi Zhang","Wenyu Ruan","Xiaojin Zhang","Zhongyu Wei","Zhenbo Luo","Jian Luan","Wei Chen","Xiang Bai"],"year":2026,"published":"2026-04-15","abstract":"Presents coarse-to-fine reasoning over multi-page documents with iterative page retrieval, evidence accumulation, and structured working memory. The evaluation targets long multi-page document VQA and provides version-independent page-level evidence-selection results.","venue":"ACL 2026"}
{"title":"Flow-Based Page Unique Semantic Mapping Architecture for Document Visual Question Answering","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2026.acl-long.1679/","doi":"10.18653/v1/2026.acl-long.1679","authors":["Haosen Wang","Jing Xiao","Chaochao Du","Xiaowang Zhang","Zhiyong Feng"],"year":2026,"abstract":"Introduces FUMA for distinguishing semantically similar document pages and localizing evidence through question-conditioned page representations and reversible flow-based mappings. Experiments evaluate both evidence localization and answer generation, but the localized unit is primarily the page rather than a complete page-region-cell hierarchy.","venue":"ACL 2026"}
{"title":"Reference Resolution and Context Change in Multimodal Situated Dialogue for Exploring Data Visualizations","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2209.02215","arxiv_id":"2209.02215","authors":["Abhinav Kumar","Barbara Di Eugenio","Abari Bhattacharya","Jillian Aurisano","Andrew Johnson"],"year":2022,"published":"2022-09-06","abstract":"Empirically studies reference resolution in multimodal dialogue where people discuss data visualizations while also using gestures. The work models how referring expressions establish or revisit visual entities and supplies structurally relevant transfer evidence for grounding workplace references into visual regions."}
{"title":"Multi-modal Reference Resolution in Situated Dialogue by Integrating Linguistic and Extra-Linguistic Clues","url":"https://aclanthology.org/I11-1010/","authors":["Ryu Iida","Masaaki Yasuhara","Takenobu Tokunaga"],"year":2011,"abstract":"Combines linguistic context with extra-linguistic visual information for resolving references in situated dialogue. The empirical task requires linking referring expressions to entities in the shared visual environment, making it transfer evidence for attachment-region reference resolution.","venue":"IJCNLP 2011"}
{"title":"Performance Evaluation and Error Analysis for Multimodal Reference Resolution in a Conversation System","url":"https://aclanthology.org/N04-4011/","authors":["Joyce Y. Chai","Zahar Prasov","Pengyu Hong"],"year":2004,"abstract":"Evaluates multimodal reference resolution in a conversational system and analyzes errors arising from combining language with nonlinguistic input. It provides early empirical evidence on resolving references to visually or interactively available entities.","venue":"HLT-NAACL 2004"}
{"title":"What You See is What You Get: Visual Pronoun Coreference Resolution in Dialogues","url":"https://aclanthology.org/D19-1516/","authors":["Xintong Yu","Hongming Zhang","Yangqiu Song","Yan Song","Changshui Zhang"],"year":2019,"abstract":"Introduces visual pronoun coreference resolution, where pronouns in dialogue are linked to visible entities rather than only textual antecedents. The associated dataset and experiments provide transfer evidence for cross-modal coreference to localized visual referents.","venue":"EMNLP-IJCNLP 2019"}
{"title":"Dual Attention Networks for Visual Reference Resolution in Visual Dialog","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/D19-1209","doi":"10.18653/v1/D19-1209","authors":["Gi-Cheon Kang","Jaeseo Lim","Byoung-Tak Zhang"],"year":2019,"abstract":"Models visual reference resolution in dialogue with dedicated mechanisms for finding and referring to visually grounded entities. The method is empirically evaluated in visual-dialog settings and serves as transfer evidence for multimodal referring-expression grounding.","venue":"EMNLP-IJCNLP 2019"}
{"title":"GRAVL-BERT: Graphical Visual-Linguistic Representations for Multimodal Coreference Resolution","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2022.coling-1.22/","authors":["Danfeng Guo","Arpit Gupta","Sanchit Agarwal","Jiun-Yu Kao","Shuyang Gao","Arijit Biswas","Chien-Wei Lin","Tagyoung Chung","Mohit Bansal"],"year":2022,"abstract":"Represents dialogue, scene objects, and their relationships jointly for multimodal coreference resolution. Experiments require linking language mentions to visual objects across conversational context, offering transfer evidence for grounding message references to structured visual entities.","venue":"COLING 2022"}
{"title":"Resolving References in Visually-Grounded Dialogue via Text Generation","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2023.sigdial-1.43/","authors":["Bram Willemsen","Livia Qian","Gabriel Skantze"],"year":2023,"abstract":"Resolves visually grounded references by generating a definite description from dialogue context and using a vision-language model to identify the corresponding visual referent. The approach is evaluated on manually annotated visually grounded dialogue data.","venue":"SIGDIAL 2023"}
{"title":"J-CRe3: A Japanese Conversation Dataset for Real-world Reference Resolution","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2024.lrec-main.829/","authors":["Nobuhiro Ueda","Hideko Habe","Akishige Yuguchi","Seiya Kawano","Yasutomo Kawanishi","Sadao Kurohashi","Koichiro Yoshino"],"year":2024,"abstract":"Provides conversational data in which linguistic referring expressions are linked across modalities to real-world objects represented by bounding boxes. It covers direct and indirect references and supplies empirical transfer evidence for language-to-region grounding.","venue":"LREC-COLING 2024"}
{"title":"Visual Grounding for User Interfaces","url":"https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/2024.naacl-industry.9","doi":"10.18653/v1/2024.naacl-industry.9","authors":["Yijun Qian","Yujie Lu","Alexander G. Hauptmann","Oriana Riva"],"year":2024,"abstract":"Takes a user-interface screenshot together with a free-form referring expression and identifies the interface element denoted by that expression. The method incorporates layout information and is empirically evaluated on screenshot grounding, making it structurally close transfer evidence for references such as highlighted or nearby screen regions.","venue":"NAACL 2024 Industry Track"}
{"title":"SeeClick: Harnessing GUI Grounding for Advanced Visual GUI Agents","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.10935","arxiv_id":"2401.10935","authors":["Kanzhi Cheng","Qiushi Sun","Yougang Chu","Fangzhi Xu","Yantao Li","Jianbing Zhang","Zhiyong Wu"],"year":2024,"published":"2024-01-17","abstract":"Trains a vision-language model to ground natural-language instructions directly to locations in GUI screenshots and introduces evaluation for GUI grounding. Although the surface is an interactive interface rather than a workplace attachment, the task directly tests expression-to-screen-region localization."}
{"title":"Ferret-UI: Grounded Mobile UI Understanding with Multimodal LLMs","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.05719","arxiv_id":"2404.05719","authors":["Keen You","Haotian Zhang","Eldon Schoop","Floris Weers","Amanda Swearngin","Jeffrey Nichols","Yinfei Yang","Zhe Gan"],"year":2024,"published":"2024-04-08","abstract":"Extends region-level multimodal understanding to mobile UI screenshots with tasks including referring, grounding, and reasoning over interface regions. Its region annotations and empirical benchmarks provide transfer evidence for expression-to-region grounding on structured screenshots."}
{"title":"Navigating the Digital World as Humans Do: Universal Visual Grounding for GUI Agents","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2410.05243","arxiv_id":"2410.05243","authors":["Boyu Gou","Ruohan Wang","Boyuan Zheng","Yanan Xie","Cheng Chang","Yiheng Shu","Huan Sun","Yu Su"],"year":2024,"published":"2024-10-07","abstract":"Studies universal GUI grounding from natural-language references to elements in screenshots and builds large-scale training data from GUI elements and referring expressions. Evaluation across multiple GUI grounding benchmarks provides broad transfer evidence for language-to-region grounding on structured visual surfaces."}
{"title":"Data Provenance: Some Basic Issues","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/3-540-44450-5_6","doi":"10.1007/3-540-44450-5_6","authors":["Peter Buneman","Sanjeev Khanna","Wang-Chiew Tan"],"year":2000,"published":"2000-12-01","abstract":"Formulates foundational questions about tracking the origins and movement of data through transformations and databases. It supplies conceptual transfer foundations for fine-grained provenance but does not itself validate multimodal document-version lineage.","venue":"Foundations of Software Technology and Theoretical Computer Science (FST TCS 2000)"}
{"title":"Provenance Semirings","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/1265530.1265535","doi":"10.1145/1265530.1265535","authors":["Todd J. Green","Grigoris Karvounarakis","Val Tannen"],"year":2007,"abstract":"Introduces a general algebraic framework in which provenance annotations are propagated through relational queries. The representation provides transfer foundations for compositional lineage of derived values, although its empirical domain is relational data rather than versioned multimodal documents.","venue":"ACM Symposium on Principles of Database Systems (PODS 2007)"}
{"title":"Tracing the lineage of view data in a warehousing environment","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/357775.357777","doi":"10.1145/357775.357777","authors":["Yingwei Cui","Jennifer Widom","Janet L. Wiener"],"year":2000,"abstract":"Defines and implements lineage tracing from derived warehouse view data back to the source data items that contributed to each result. The work handles query transformations including aggregation and provides transfer evidence for fine-grained derived-value-to-source provenance.","venue":"ACM Transactions on Database Systems"}
{"title":"Provenance Management in Curated Databases","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/1142473.1142534","doi":"10.1145/1142473.1142534","authors":["Peter Buneman","Adriane Chapman","James Cheney"],"year":2006,"abstract":"Presents a provenance-management approach for curated databases that records user copying and modification actions and connects provenance with version history. The implementation demonstrates how provenance can be retained as data is repeatedly curated and revised, providing transfer evidence for revision-aware lineage.","venue":"ACM SIGMOD International Conference on Management of Data 2006"}
